        "original_id": "4a8d8e0d-b6e0-5c02-8585-b84b4fe631e1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Dawn French, Jennifer Saunders, Adrian Edmondson, Keith Allen, Nigel Planer, Alexei Sayle, Ronald Allen, Robbie Coltrane, Alan \"Al\" Pillay, Lana Pellay, Alana Pellay, Alan Pellay, Gary Clail\n- Works: The Supergrass, French and Saunders, The Vicar of Dibley, Eat the Rich, The Comic Strip Presents, Gino, Human Nature, Emotional Hooligan\n- Roles: actress, writer, comedian, backing vocalist\n\nFacts:\n- Dawn Roma French was born on 11 October 1957 and is an English actress, writer, and comedian.\n- Dawn French is best known for starring in and writing for French and Saunders with comedy partner Jennifer Saunders.\n- Dawn French is also known for playing Geraldine Granger in The Vicar of Dibley.\n- Alan \"Al\" Pillay was born on 22 August 1959 and is also known as Al Pillay.\n- Alan \"Al\" Pillay starred in Eat the Rich.\n- In The Comic Strip Presents episode Gino, Alan \"Al\" Pillay appeared as Alan Pellay playing himself.\n- In The Comic Strip Presents episode 13, Alan \"Al\" Pillay appeared as Alana Pellay playing herself.\n- Alan \"Al\" Pillay appeared as Lana Pellay playing Mary in the feature film The Supergrass.\n- The film The Supergrass starred Richardson, Adrian Edmondson, Jennifer Saunders, Dawn French, Keith Allen, Nigel Planer, Alexei Sayle, Ronald Allen, and Robbie Coltrane.\n- The song Human Nature by Gary Clail On-U Sound System features Lana Pellay on backing vocals.\n- Human Nature can be found on the album Emotional Hooligan.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
